## System tray support on Linux (StatusNotifierItem)

### Overview

Add a system tray icon on Linux using the [`ksni`](https://crates.io/crates/ksni) crate,
which implements the `org.kde.StatusNotifierItem` D-Bus protocol — the modern standard
supported by KDE Plasma, GNOME (with AppIndicator extension), XFCE (via snixembed), and others.

No GTK or Qt dependency is required. `ksni` integrates cleanly with an existing
tokio multi-thread runtime, which rqbit already uses.

### Cargo.toml
```toml
[dependencies]
ksni = "0.3"
```

### Implementation
```rust
// src/tray.rs

use std::sync::mpsc;

#[derive(Debug)]
pub enum TrayCmd {
    ShowWindow,
    Quit,
}

#[derive(Debug)]
struct RqbitTray {
    tx: mpsc::SyncSender<TrayCmd>,
}

impl ksni::Tray for RqbitTray {
    // Left click opens the menu instead of calling activate() directly.
    // This is the expected behavior on most Linux DEs.
    const MENU_ON_ACTIVATE: bool = true;

    fn id(&self) -> String { "rqbit".into() }
    fn title(&self) -> String { "rqbit".into() }
    fn category(&self) -> ksni::Category { ksni::Category::ApplicationStatus }
    fn status(&self) -> ksni::Status { ksni::Status::Active }

    // Uses the system icon theme (hicolor / Papirus / etc.)
    fn icon_name(&self) -> String { "network-transmit-receive".into() }

    fn menu(&self) -> Vec<ksni::MenuItem<Self>> {
        use ksni::menu::*;
        vec![
            StandardItem {
                label: "Open rqbit".into(),
                icon_name: "window-restore".into(),
                activate: Box::new(|t: &mut Self| {
                    let _ = t.tx.send(TrayCmd::ShowWindow);
                }),
                ..Default::default()
            }.into(),
            MenuItem::Separator,
            StandardItem {
                label: "Quit".into(),
                icon_name: "application-exit".into(),
                activate: Box::new(|t: &mut Self| {
                    let _ = t.tx.send(TrayCmd::Quit);
                }),
                ..Default::default()
            }.into(),
        ]
    }

    // Reconnect automatically if the DE restarts its StatusNotifierWatcher
    fn watcher_offline(&self, reason: ksni::OfflineReason) -> bool {
        eprintln!("[tray] watcher offline ({reason:?}), retrying");
        true
    }
}

pub struct AppTray {
    rx: mpsc::Receiver<TrayCmd>,
    _handle: ksni::Handle<RqbitTray>,
}

impl AppTray {
    /// Call this from within a tokio async context (e.g. inside #[tokio::main]).
    pub async fn spawn() -> anyhow::Result<Self> {
        let (tx, rx) = mpsc::sync_channel::<TrayCmd>(8);
        use ksni::TrayMethods;
        let handle = RqbitTray { tx }.spawn().await
            .map_err(|e| anyhow::anyhow!("tray spawn failed: {e}"))?;
        Ok(Self { rx, _handle: handle })
    }

    /// Non-blocking poll — call from your main loop or a timer.
    /// Returns (show_window, quit).
    pub fn poll(&self) -> (bool, bool) {
        let (mut show, mut quit) = (false, false);
        while let Ok(cmd) = self.rx.try_recv() {
            match cmd {
                TrayCmd::ShowWindow => show = true,
                TrayCmd::Quit      => quit = true,
            }
        }
        (show, quit)
    }
}
```

### Usage
```rust
#[tokio::main]
async fn main() {
    // Only register tray if a D-Bus session is available
    let tray = if std::env::var("DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS").is_ok() {
        match AppTray::spawn().await {
            Ok(t)  => { eprintln!("[tray] registered"); Some(t) }
            Err(e) => { eprintln!("[tray] unavailable: {e}"); None }
        }
    } else {
        None
    };

    // In your event/polling loop:
    if let Some(ref tray) = tray {
        let (show, quit) = tray.poll();
        if show { /* bring window to front */ }
        if quit { /* graceful shutdown */ }
    }
}
```

### Notes

- **`ksni` spawns its own async task** for D-Bus communication — no extra threads needed
- **`std::sync::mpsc`** (not tokio mpsc) is intentional — avoids deadlocks when polling from a sync context
- **`MENU_ON_ACTIVATE = true`** — left click shows the menu rather than calling `activate()` directly.
  This is important for correct behavior across DEs:
  - **KDE Plasma** — works natively with SNI
  - **GNOME** — requires the [AppIndicator and KStatusNotifierItem Support](https://extensions.gnome.org/extension/615/appindicator-support/) shell extension
  - **XFCE** — requires [snixembed](https://github.com/nicowillis/snixembed) to bridge the legacy XEmbed tray to SNI; `MENU_ON_ACTIVATE = true` is necessary here as left click behavior differs
- **`watcher_offline → true`** — tray icon survives DE restarts and shell crashes without restarting the app

